as 0x40, which requires A0 to be tied low (GND).\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40 | FCCPeripherals.sch note \\\"PWM Driver\\\"\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"FCC Peripherals sheet: A0 pin 1 wired to +3.3V; note 'I2C address: 0x41'\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The PWM driver answers at 0x41 rather than 0x40, so firmware written for the specified address will not communicate with it.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely deviation is the NAVC NRST pin sitting on net NET0054 instead of the reset-switch net NET0051, which would leave the NAVC unresettable by its button and debug header. The PCA9685 A0 strap to +3.3V (address 0x41) against the spec's 0x40 is a lower-confidence second candidate.\"\n}",
